+# Spike 0004 code
+
+Harness for `openintent/experiments/spikes/0004-guarded-scratch-merge-sync/report.md`. None of this is product code, and it is never merged: it exists only to answer that report's question and it lands beside the report as `evidence.patch`.
+
+## Files
+
+| Path | What it is |
+| --- | --- |
+| `sync-upstream.sh` | The thing under test: the guarded scratch-merge sync, steps (1) to (6) of the frozen definition. |
+| `lib.sh` | Disposable Pi worktrees from `frozen-at`, the port step, Git's automatic result, directory comparison, and the run wrapper (own process group, closed stdin, 60-second alarm). |
+| `chain.sh` | C1: R1 to R5 in order; records the state after R5. |
+| `single.sh` | C2 and C3: R6 and K1. |
+| `uptodate-u2.sh` | C4, case U2. |
+| `guards.sh` | C4 (U1), C5 (G1, G4), C6 (G2a, G2b) and C7 (G3), each from a fresh worktree at the state after R5. |
+| `all.sh` | Every case, with the fork working trees' status before and after. |
+| `runs/` | Raw output, one file per case. |
+| `findings/sync.md` | Per-claim conclusions. |
+
+## Running it
+
+From the worktree root, with pi-claude-bridge at `edf19ed` and rpiv-mono at `8403bb09`, each with the `upstream/main` the report's versions table names:
+
+```
+spike/all.sh
+```
+
+The harness writes only under `/tmp`, in disposable worktrees of the Pi repository, and in `spike/runs/`. No harness calls a model or fetches.
