+# Guarded scratch-merge sync findings
+
+No subagent ran a harness; the coordinator read every claim from the run files below. Every sync ran with stdin from `/dev/null`, no terminal, its own process group and a 60-second alarm.
+
+| Claim | Result | Status | Run files |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| C1 | R1 to R5: five base matches; conflicted sets of 11, 14, 11, 4 and 13 files equal Git's; every comparison identical; exit 1 each time. | proved | `runs/R1.txt` to `runs/R5.txt` |
+| C2 | R6: base match, one conflicted file (`CHANGELOG.md`) equal to Git's, comparison identical, exit 1. | proved | `runs/R6.txt` |
+| C3 | K1: no conflicted file, comparison identical, exit 0 with `SYNC OUTCOME: clean`. | proved | `runs/K1.txt` |
+| C4 | U1: exit 3, `git status --porcelain --ignored` empty, `HEAD` unchanged. U2: exit 3, only `UPSTREAM.json`'s base line differs. | proved | `runs/U1.txt`, `runs/U2.txt` |
+| C5 | G1 and G4: exit 2 with the ancestry refusal (Git exits 1 and 128), status empty, `HEAD` unchanged. | proved | `runs/G1.txt`, `runs/G4.txt` |
+| C6 | G2a and G2b: exit 2 naming the trailer mismatch (none, then the stale `0750748`), status empty, `HEAD` unchanged. | proved | `runs/G2a.txt`, `runs/G2b.txt` |
+| C7 | G3: exit 2 naming the uncommitted changes; `README.md` unchanged; `HEAD` unchanged. | proved | `runs/G3.txt` |
+| C8 | Exit codes 0, 1, 2 and 3 with the status lines "clean", "conflicts (n files)", "refused (…)" and "up to date"; every run under 1 second; no survivor in any process group. | proved | the `sync-exit` and `survivors` lines of every run file |
+| C9 | Every run lists no status entry outside its package directory; both fork working trees show the same status before and after. | proved | the containment lines of every run file, `runs/00-fork-status.txt` |
+| C10 | After R1 to R5 and K1, no result path is missing from the index, and `TODO.md` is tracked. | proved | `runs/R1.txt` to `runs/R5.txt`, `runs/K1.txt` |
+
+Supporting, proved by the named runs:
+
+- Before each chain step, the Pi side equals the fork state before the sync (`runs/R1.txt` to `runs/R5.txt`).
+- The state after R5 is commit `d966ade3fab29644ce5f0ccc90cb8b6566d1a444` in the object store the disposable worktrees share (`runs/state-after-R5.txt`).
+- All disposable Pi worktrees are removed and pruned (`runs/00-fork-status.txt`).
